    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Vector Equation of a Straight Line Given Parametrically",
    "problem": "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=13-8t \\\\ y=7t \\\\ z=-7-3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?",
    "worked_solution": "These parametric equations are equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13-8t \\\\ 7t \\\\ -7-3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-8t \\\\ 7t \\\\ -3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$",
